# Architecture

Stack: Next.js 14+ App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, React Three Fiber.

- Strict TypeScript. No `any`. Type props, variants, params, and loader props explicitly.
- Semantic HTML5 (`header`, `main`, `section`, `nav`, `article`, `footer`) inside motion wrappers.
- One route segment per service under `app/services/`, or a typed dynamic route `app/services/[slug]/page.tsx` fed by a typed catalog. Do not render every service from a single page component.

```tsx
type ServicePageProps = {
  params: { slug: string };
};

export default function ServicePage({ params }: ServicePageProps) {
  return (
    <main>
      <motion.article transition={{ type: "spring", stiffness: 100, damping: 15 }}>
        {params.slug}
      </motion.article>
    </main>
  );
}
```
